e unspecified. Copper availability, sulfide speciation, UV penetration and intermediate residence times also remain environmental implementation questions.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_007"], "suggestions": ["Attach reaction-specific references and operating conditions, distinguishing lactonitrile experiments from representative experiments on other nitriles.", "Specify photoredox catalyst availability, sulfur speciation, light exposure and intermediate handling.", "Provide aminonitrile hydrolysis conditions and kinetics demonstrating free-threonine release faster than competing degradation."]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_001": 0.97, "rxn_003": 0.74, "rxn_005": 0.95, "rxn_006": 0.93, "rxn_007": 0.83}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.82, "pathway_coherence": 0.9, "environmental_progression": 0.68, "target_achievement": 0.73, "overall_confidence": 0.78, "feedback": "This is a coherent implementation variant, not an independently established threonine mechanism. The supplied literature supports copper-free sulfide photochemistry in the broader network, but does not establish equivalent lactonitrile-to-lactaldehyde performance for rxn_003. The network appropriately labels this extrapolation. Removing copper does not by itself resolve sulfide availability, UV attenuation or the final hydrolysis bottleneck.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_003", "rxn_007"], "suggestions": ["Measure substrate-specific lactaldehyde yield and competing products under copper-free irradiation.", "Define sulfide concentration, pH, irradiation spectrum and exposure time without importing performance from the copper-assisted experiment.", "Validate downstream aminonitrile hydrolysis and threonine survival under specified surface conditions."]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_001": 0.97, "rxn_004": 0.73, "rxn_005": 0.95, "rxn_006": 0.93, "rxn_007": 0.83}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.81, "pathway_coherence": 0.9, "environmental_prog