y HCN concentration, oligomerization conditions and aminomalononitrile availability relative to competing oligomers.", "Distinguish experimentally identified intermediates from mechanistic representations.", "Provide hydrolysis/decarboxylation conditions, residence times and stereoisomer-resolved threonine recovery under an environmentally justified workup."]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_012": 0.9}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.89, "pathway_coherence": 0.88, "environmental_progression": 0.78, "target_achievement": 0.86, "overall_confidence": 0.85, "feedback": "Ivanov and Ivanov (1983) provide direct support for threonine formation in glycine/aldehyde chemistry at pH 3.3-3.7 and 60-80 degrees C without inorganic solids. The balanced edge is acceptable as a net product-forming channel, not as evidence for a selective elementary reaction. Within this network, glycine is supplied by other branches rather than declared as an external starting material, so this pathway depends on their delivery of an accessible glycine pool. Yield, competing products and threonine persistence remain unquantified.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": [], "suggestions": ["Encode the experimentally supported pH and temperature window, together with substrate concentrations and reaction duration.", "Specify how network-produced glycine and acetaldehyde reach the reaction conditions without excessive loss.", "Report threonine yield and product distributions without assuming either exclusive threonine formation or an established threonine:allothreonine ratio."]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_013": 0.71}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.72, "pathway_coherence": 0.76, "environmental_progression": 0.74, "target_achievement": 0.68, "overall_confidence": 0.73, "feedback": "The supplied literature supports oligoglycine-aldehyde chemistry, but not necessarily the exact glycylglycine-plus-acetaldehyde transformation and product release represented here. The net equation is conservation-valid, and the network appropriately identifies diglycine as a provisional proxy. The unresolved issues are substrate specificity, the site and sequence of modification, and peptide hydrolysis or amino-acid release under the stated conditions.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_013"], "suggestions": ["Establish whether glycylglycine itself was experimentally tested before assigning oligoglycine evidence to this specific molecule.", "Separate or annotate peptide modification and subsequent amino-acid release while retaining uncertainty about unresolved intermediates.", "Measure free versus peptide-bound threonine and verify release kinetics under the proposed warm acidic conditions."]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_014": 0.82}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.82, "pathway_coherence": 0.77, "environmental_progression": 0.61, "target_achievement": 0.75, "overall_confidence": 0.74, "feedback": "Historical HCN/ammonia experiments, including Matthews and Moser, support threonine detection after hydrolysis of complex reaction products. Representing this as an ensemble is appropriate and avoids inventing an elementary mechanism. Nevertheless, high cyanide concentrations and strong-acid hydrolysis are substantial implementation requirements. The balance-check coefficients establish conservation only; they do not establish the actual product distribution or measured ensemble stoichiometry.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_014"], "suggestions": ["Specify a physically supported cyanide concentration and retention process.", "Annotate precursor formation and analytical hydrolysis as distinct stages, without inventing a unique molecular precursor.", "Provide environmental hydrolysis kinetics and measured yields rather than interpreting balanceable coefficients as production ratios."]}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_015": 0.81}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.82, "pathway_coherence": 0.77, "environmental_